msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:67
msgid "Label texts that must be followed by visible non-blank text — catches bindings that resolve to empty (numeric 0, \"0\", null and \"\" all render blank)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:74
#: includes/features.php:872
msgid "Check rendered output"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:75
msgid "Fetches one front-end page as the invoking user (an authenticated loopback — logged-in users see saved dev-branch commits, so no publish is needed) and scans the HTML for the dynamic-data failures that save-time validation cannot catch: leaked <template> elements, unresolved [[...]] or {{...}} bindings, PHP warnings/fatals, missing expected text, unexpectedly present text, and labels with blank values. Interactive (client-side URL-source) Collections are exempt from the template/binding scan — their markup legitimately ships to the browser. A saved data variable with a bad nested field, a scalar Collection source or a runtime resolver failure all pass dbe/manage-data-variable but fail here — run this after every dynamic-data save. Pass page (post ID or path) or a same-site url, plus optional query args."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:83
msgid "WordPress post ID or path (e.g. \"dbe-dynamic-stress\" or \"/events/\") to fetch. Use this OR url."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:87
#: includes/abilities-verify.php:135
msgid "Full same-site URL to fetch. Other hosts are refused."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:92
msgid "Query parameters to append, e.g. {\"topic\": \"dbe-stress-build\", \"listing_page\": \"2\"}."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:107
msgid "Each failure: check, message, and up to five matches with line numbers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:122
#: includes/features.php:877
msgid "Check render scenarios"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:123
msgid "Runs dbe/check-rendered-output across a matrix of request scenarios against one page — each scenario sets its own query parameters and/or cookies and its own expectations. This is how URL-driven listings are proven: default filters, a valid override, an invalid value falling back, pagination pages, cookie-segmented content and recursive roots, in one call. Shared expect/absent/nonblank_labels apply to every scenario on top of the per-scenario ones. At most ten scenarios per call; every scenario fetch runs the full failure scan (leaked templates, unresolved bindings, PHP errors)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:131
msgid "WordPress post ID or path to fetch. Use this OR url."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:139
msgid "Up to ten scenarios. Each: { label, query?: {name: value}, cookies?: {name: value}, expect?: [], absent?: [], nonblank_labels?: [] }."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:181
msgid "Per scenario: label, url, status_code, passed and failures."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:195
msgid "WordPress post ID or path establishing the resolution context (current post, archive, URL parameters). Defaults to the site front page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:199
msgid "Full same-site URL establishing the context instead of page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:204
msgid "Query parameters for the context request — url_parameter() resolvers read these."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:211
msgid "Get the dynamic-data GraphQL schema"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:212
msgid "Returns the LIVE Builderius dynamic-data GraphQL schema — the Root query type every data variable runs against, including fields added by Builderius Pro, ACF, Meta Box and other integrations on this site. No open builder tab is needed. By default returns the Root fields (name, arguments, return type) and an index of type names; pass type to expand one type's fields, or search to find fields/types by name fragment. Use this instead of guessing field names: a wrong nested field saves fine but silently blanks the whole variable at render."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:219
msgid "A type name to expand (e.g. Post, User, Term, Pagination). Case-sensitive."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:223
msgid "Case-insensitive fragment matched against type and field names (e.g. \"acf\", \"meta\", \"pagination\")."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:228
msgid "Bypass the cached schema (use after activating a plugin that extends it)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:238
msgid "The Root query fields: name, args, type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:243
msgid "The expanded type (name, kind, fields) when type was passed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:247
msgid "Search hits as \"Type.field: ReturnType\" rows when search was passed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:265
#: includes/features.php:857
msgid "Resolve a data variable"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:266
msgid "Validates AND actually resolves one dynamic-data variable, returning its runtime value in a chosen page context — the missing proof step between \"the query saved\" and \"the page renders\". The query is first validated against the live GraphQL schema (unknown fields and bad arguments are reported with messages, which dbe/manage-data-variable's syntax check cannot see), then executed through Builderius' own dynamic-data channel with the context page's real WordPress query state, so wp/current-post/url_parameter resolvers behave exactly as on the front end. Pass name for a saved variable (its [[dep]] dependencies resolve too) or graphql_query for an ad-hoc probe. Large values are compacted (lists truncated, long strings clipped) unless full: true."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:274
msgid "A saved data variable name. Global scope by default; pass template for entity scope."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:278
msgid "An ad-hoc GraphQL query to resolve instead of a saved variable. Saved global variables are still available as [[dep]] interpolations. (The query parameter carries URL parameters for the context request instead.)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:282
#: includes/abilities-verify.php:349
msgid "Template (or component) post ID or slug for ENTITY-scoped variables. Omit for the global settings set."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:288
#: includes/abilities-verify.php:355
msgid "Entity type when template is passed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:292
#: includes/abilities-verify.php:359
msgid "Global settings set post ID or slug. Omit when the site has one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:297
msgid "Return the complete value without compaction. Use only when the compact preview is not enough."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:309
msgid "Schema validation: valid plus error messages (an invalid query is still executed so you can see the runtime effect)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:312
msgid "The resolved value (compacted unless full: true; compaction is flagged in truncated)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:317
msgid "Byte length of the full JSON-encoded value."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:322
msgid "Every variable name resolved in the request (the target plus its dependencies)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:336
#: includes/features.php:862
msgid "Inspect a binding value"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:337
msgid "Reports the resolved type and compact shape at a binding path — run this on a Collection's data-b-context source BEFORE binding it, because a source that is not an array renders a silent empty loop (scalars/null leave the <template> markup in the page; an object renders exactly once). Accepts a saved-variable path (\"var.path.to.items\", with or without [[ ]]/[[[ ]]] wrapping) or a literal JSON source. Returns the value's type, list/object classification, row count, first-row keys, a small preview, and whether it is safe as a Collection source in the chosen page context."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:345
msgid "The binding to inspect: \"var.path.to.items\", \"[[var.path]]\", \"[[[var.path]]]\", or a literal JSON array/object."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:372
msgid "list | object | string | number | boolean | null | missing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:376
msgid "Whether this value is safe as a Collection source (a non-empty list of rows)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:384
msgid "Compacted value preview."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:402
#: includes/features.php:867
msgid "Resolve a Meta Box field"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:403
msgid "Maps a Meta Box field to the exact ways Builderius dynamic data can read it, so agents stop guessing: the builder's auto-generated helper name (derived from the slugified field LABEL, not the id — field id rc_number labelled \"RC Number (CAC)\" becomes wp.…__rc_number_cac_), the GraphQL accessor and arguments for headless data variables (settings-page fields need option_name, the storage owner, which is NOT always the admin page id), group children, and the array/clone caveats. Searches every registered field by id or label fragment across posts, users, terms and settings pages. Term fields get a warning: Builderius ships no term Meta Box helper and term meta_value() has returned false in testing — use a php_function_output wrapper."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:410
msgid "The field id, or a fragment of the id or label, to search for."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:415
msgid "Limit the search to one Meta Box object type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:426
msgid "Per field: id, label, type, object_type, context (post type or settings page), builder_helper, graphql read recipe, children, warnings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:431
msgid "Total matches before the 20-row cap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:444
msgid "Get a module's matched styles"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:445
msgid "Returns the authored CSS rules that target one module, gathered from the saved entity CSS and the global stylesheet — the headless stand-in for the builder's computed-styles tool when no live builder tab is connected. Rules are matched against the module's tag, id, classes and its uni-node id (per-module %local% styles compile to .uni-node-<id> selectors), with their media-query context preserved. This reports what the stylesheets SAY, not what a browser computed — cascade order and specificity are returned so you can reason about conflicts, but inherited values and runtime layout are out of scope."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:452
#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:221
msgid "Template or component post ID or slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:458
#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:227
msgid "Entity type of the template reference."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:462
msgid "The module whose matched rules to report (find ids with dbe/get-tree-outline)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:467
msgid "Also match rules from the global stylesheet (framework classes)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:478
msgid "The module's identity: id, tag, html id, classes, label."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-verify.php:482
msgid "Matched rules in source order: selector, declarations, media, source (entity|global), matched_by."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:44
msgid "Duplicate a template"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:45
msgid "Creates an isolated working copy of a Builderius template from its saved state: the module tree, entity CSS, entity-scoped data variables and JS snippets all ride along in the copied config. The copy is created DISABLED and without apply rules by default so it can never shadow the original on the front end — pass enabled: true and copy_apply_rules: true only when a live twin is genuinely wanted. Page-bound templates are duplicated as regular templates (a WordPress page can only bind one page template); hook templates keep their hook wiring. The copy starts a fresh commit history."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:52
msgid "Source template post ID or slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:56
#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:115
msgid "Title for the copy. Defaults to \"<source title> copy\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:60
#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:119
msgid "Slug for the copy. Defaults to WordPress' unique slug for the title."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:65
msgid "Enable the copy immediately. Default false: a duplicate that is live from birth can conflict with the original."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:70
msgid "Copy the source's apply rules onto the duplicate. Default false so the copy applies nowhere until deliberately targeted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:81
msgid "The duplicate's summary (id, slug, title, enabled, type, apply_rules, branch, commit)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:85
msgid "The source template (id, slug) and the commit the content was copied from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:103
msgid "Duplicate a component"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:104
msgid "Creates a copy of a Builderius component definition from its saved state: the internal module tree, declared properties (and their derived props variable), entity CSS and entity-scoped data variables all ride along. The copy gets a fresh slug and commit history; existing instances keep pointing at the source component. Use this to fork a shared component before an experiment instead of editing the shared original in place."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:111
msgid "Source component post ID or slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:130
msgid "The duplicate's summary (id, slug, title, props, branch, commit)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:134
msgid "The source component (id, slug) and the commit the content was copied from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:148
msgid "List global settings sets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:149
msgid "Enumerates the site's Builderius global settings sets — the entities that carry the framework CSS, global data variables and global JS snippets. Most sites have exactly one; when several exist, the global CSS and data-variable abilities need a settings_set reference, and this ability is how an agent discovers the right one. Each row reports the set's identity, saved commit (for the expected_commit save flow), stylesheet size, named CSS blocks, and how many global data variables and JS snippets it holds."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:161
msgid "Per set: id, slug, title, technology, branch_id, commit_name, css_length, css_blocks, data_variables, js_snippets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:175
#: includes/features.php:892
msgid "Validate a JS snippet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:176
msgid "Structurally validates JavaScript before it is saved with dbe/manage-js-snippet: unbalanced brackets/braces/parentheses, unterminated strings, template literals, comments and regular expressions, and stray HTML are reported with line numbers. This is a structural scan, not a full ECMAScript parse — code that passes can still contain runtime or semantic errors, so treat a pass as \"safe to save\", not \"proven correct\". Nothing is saved or executed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:183
msgid "The JavaScript source to check."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:195
msgid "Structural problems found, each with a message and line number."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:200
msgid "The level of validation performed (structural)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:213
msgid "Manage an element's rendering conditions"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:214
msgid "Reads, sets or clears one element's rendering (visibility) conditions in the saved state — the setting dbe/apply-subtree-html preserves through data-dbe-id markers but cannot express in HTML. Conditions are OR-of-AND groups: pass groups as an array of arrays, each inner array a set of AND-ed rules { name, operator, value } and the outer array OR-ed — e.g. [[{\"name\":\"user_logged_in\",\"operator\":\"is\",\"value\":\"true\"}]] shows the element to logged-in users only. Rule names and operators are validated against Builderius' installed rendering-condition registry (post_type, user_role, url_parameter, is_front_page, dynamic_data, expression, …). Conditions that read the wp system variable (post_type, post_meta, user_role, …) need matching fields in the wp query — the result warns when they look absent, because the builder maintains those automatically and this channel cannot; always prove the element with dbe/check-rendered-output afterwards. Alternatively pass expression for a raw Twig-style condition string. Use action: get first to read the current shape; set replaces the whole condition; clear removes it (the element always renders)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:231
msgid "The element's module ID (find it with dbe/get-tree-outline)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:236
msgid "get reads, set replaces, clear removes the condition."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:240
msgid "For set: OR-ed groups, each an array of AND-ed rules { name, operator, value }. Omit value only for is_empty/is_not_empty operators."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:249
msgid "The comparison value. key_value widgets (post_meta, user_meta, url_parameter, cookie) take \"key:value\" strings."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:259
msgid "For set: a raw condition expression string instead of groups (stored verbatim, evaluated by Builderius' expression engine)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:264
msgid "Preview the condition value that WOULD be saved without committing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:268
msgid "The active commit name from the preceding read. Required when saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:273
#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:358
msgid "Explicitly override a dirty Builderius-tab conflict."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:284
msgid "The condition value (current for get, resulting for set/clear)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:304
msgid "Manage a global settings set"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:305
msgid "Reads or updates the global settings set's non-CSS settings: the responsive strategy (desktop-first/mobile-first), the named breakpoints behind @media (--tablet)-style queries, and the font declarations. Builderius creates exactly one set per technology automatically, so there is no create or delete — use dbe/list-settings-sets to discover the sets and dbe/get-global-css / dbe/patch-global-css for the stylesheet itself. Changing breakpoints affects EVERY template's responsive CSS; changing the responsive strategy flips which direction the breakpoint media queries cascade — treat both as site-wide design decisions, read first with action: get, and save with the expected_commit flow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:312
#: includes/abilities.php:457
msgid "Global settings set post ID or slug. Omit when the site has one (the usual case)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:317
msgid "get reads the settings; update writes the passed fields as a new commit."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:322
msgid "For update: the responsive strategy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:326
msgid "For update: the COMPLETE breakpoints list, replacing the current one. Each: { name: \"--tablet\", label, width, width_builder?, icon?, deletable? }."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:343
msgid "For update: the COMPLETE font declarations list, replacing the current one. Each: { type, content }."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:349
msgid "Preview the resulting settings without committing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:353
msgid "The active commit name from the preceding get. Required when saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities-workflow.php:369
msgid "Identity: id, slug, title, technology."
msgstr ""

