#: includes/abilities.php:380
msgid "The published release (id, version, status); null on a dry run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:385
msgid "The templates included (id, slug, saved commit)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:400
#: includes/features.php:988
msgid "Extract a release (work on a release)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:401
msgid "Rebuilds the DEVELOPMENT state from a Builderius release — the builder's \"work on a release\" action, via the same extractRelease mutation. Builderius first DELETES every existing template, component and global settings set (framework CSS and all commit history included), then recreates each entity from the release's bundled configs with a fresh single-commit history. The release itself is untouched and stays published, so logged-out visitors see no change. Use when development state is missing or meaningless while a release exists — the classic case is a migrated site whose builder shows empty templates although the live pages render fine — or to roll development back to what is published. This destroys ALL unpublished work; requires confirm: true after explicit user approval. Always run with dry_run first: it reports the release contents and everything that would be deleted. Close open builder tabs before extracting and reload them afterwards — a stale tab's save would resurrect deleted state."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:408
msgid "Builderius release post ID, version/title, or slug to extract. Omit for the latest published release."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:413
msgid "Preview only: report the release contents and the current entities that WOULD be deleted, without extracting."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:418
msgid "Must be true to extract. Extraction permanently replaces all development state; confirm with the user first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:429
msgid "The release being extracted (id, version, date)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:433
msgid "The release's bundled entities (slug, name, entity_type, type) that extraction recreates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:438
msgid "Slugs of the current templates, components and settings_sets that extraction deletes first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:442
msgid "Slugs of the templates, components and settings_sets present after extraction; null on a dry run."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:463
#: includes/features.php:812
msgid "Get global CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:464
msgid "Reads the site's saved global CSS — the ENTIRE framework stylesheet (reset, design tokens, utility classes), which the builder's update_global_css tool REPLACES wholesale rather than appending to. Returns the raw CSS plus the names of its named blocks (regions fenced by /* @block: name */ … /* @endblock */ comments). Pass block to fetch just one block's body instead of the whole stylesheet. To add or change CSS safely, prefer dbe/patch-global-css, which edits only a named block and can never clobber the framework."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:472
#: includes/abilities.php:568
msgid "Return only this named block's body (token-cheap)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:500
msgid "Patch global CSS (named block)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:501
msgid "Adds, replaces or deletes ONE named block in the global stylesheet — a region fenced by /* @block: name */ … /* @endblock */ — and saves the result as a new commit. Every byte outside the named block is preserved verbatim, so unlike update_global_css this can never wipe the framework. A block that does not exist yet is appended at the end of the stylesheet. Typical use: a \"fonts\" block holding @font-face rules plus a :root override of --heading-font-family / --body-font-family. Saving does not publish; run dbe/publish for the change to reach logged-out visitors (a logged-in user already sees saved commits)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:509
#: includes/abilities.php:611
msgid "The block name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:513
#: includes/abilities.php:615
msgid "The block's new body (omit when deleting)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:518
#: includes/abilities.php:620
msgid "Remove the block entirely."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:523
#: includes/abilities.php:625
msgid "Preview: return the action and resulting stylesheet length without saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:542
#: includes/abilities.php:643
msgid "The new commit (absent on a dry run)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:558
#: includes/features.php:817
msgid "Get entity CSS"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:559
msgid "Reads a template's saved entity CSS (the per-template stylesheet the builder's update_entity_css tool replaces wholesale). Returns the raw CSS plus the names of its named blocks (regions fenced by /* @block: name */ … /* @endblock */ comments). Pass block to fetch just one block's body. A template with no entity CSS returns an empty string, not an error. To add or change CSS safely, prefer dbe/patch-entity-css, which edits only a named block."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:600
msgid "Patch entity CSS (named block)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:601
msgid "Adds, replaces or deletes ONE named block in a template's entity CSS — a region fenced by /* @block: name */ … /* @endblock */ — and saves the result as a new commit through Builderius' own save channel, without touching the open builder store. CSS outside the named block is preserved verbatim. A block that does not exist yet is appended at the end; a template with no entity CSS at all gets one created. CAUTION: if a builder tab has that template open with unsaved changes, saving or closing that tab afterwards can overwrite this commit with the tab's stale copy — save or discard the tab first. Saving does not publish; run dbe/publish for the change to reach logged-out visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:662
msgid "List saved commits"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:663
msgid "Lists the saved commits of a template or of the global settings set (target \"global\"), newest first: name, date, description and — for the global set — each commit's stylesheet length, so a framework-clobbering save stands out as a sudden size drop. Use with dbe/restore-global-css-from-commit to roll the global CSS back to a pre-damage snapshot."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:670
msgid "\"global\" (default) for the global settings set, or a template post ID/slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:675
msgid "Maximum commits to return."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:690
msgid "The active commit's name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:703
#: includes/features.php:965
msgid "Restore global CSS from a commit"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:704
msgid "Recovery for a clobbered global stylesheet: reads the `css` setting from an earlier commit of the global settings set (find one with dbe/list-commits — a healthy framework is tens of KB) and saves it as a NEW commit, so the rollback is itself in history. Nothing else from the old commit is restored. Saving does not publish; run dbe/publish for the recovered CSS to reach logged-out visitors."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:711
msgid "The source commit name (from dbe/list-commits)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:716
msgid "Preview: return the source stylesheet's length and first lines without saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:730
msgid "The new commit holding the restored CSS (absent on a dry run)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:736
msgid "First lines of the restored stylesheet (dry run only)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:750
msgid "Where the template applies: { \"location\": name, \"conditions\": rules }. Core locations: front_page, home, singulars, blog_posts, pages, archives, 404, entire_site; Pro adds custom_posts, post_type_archives, taxonomy_archives, tag_archives, author_archives, date/year/month/day_archives, search_results, attachment_posts. Conditions follow Builderius' rule tree, e.g. {\"condition\":\"or\",\"rules\":[{\"condition\":\"and\",\"rules\":[{\"name\":\"post_id\",\"operator\":\"equals\",\"value\":3}]}]}. Pass null to clear the rules (the template then applies nowhere)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:772
#: includes/features.php:827
msgid "Get template settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:773
msgid "Reads a Builderius template's registration-level settings — title, slug, enabled state, type, technology, sort order and apply rules (location + conditions) — plus its branch and saved commit. These are the settings the builder's template dialog edits, not the module tree (dbe/get-subtree-html) or CSS (dbe/get-entity-css). Omit template to list every template."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:780
msgid "Template post ID or slug. Omit for all templates."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:803
msgid "Create a template"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:804
msgid "Creates a Builderius template through the builder's own mutations, headlessly — no builder tab needed. Builderius initialises the master branch and an initial commit (site header/footer components, a <main> element and a default `wp` data variable), so dbe/get-subtree-html and dbe/apply-subtree-html work on it immediately. Type page uses the builder's createPageTemplate: pass page_id instead of a title — the title, slug and apply rule (that one page) all derive from the WP page or enabled custom-post; other inputs then act as post-create overrides. Types beyond regular/page/hook (e.g. doc) are created as regular and re-termed, matching the builder's behaviour. A non-page template is created enabled but applies nowhere until apply_rules is set (here or later via dbe/update-template). Creating never publishes; the new template reaches logged-out visitors only after dbe/publish."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:811
msgid "Template title, shown in the builder's template list. Must be unique. Required unless page_id is passed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:815
msgid "Slug. Defaults to a sanitised form of the title. Must be unique."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:820
msgid "Template type: regular, page (needs page_id), doc or hook (needs the hook fields below)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:824
msgid "Page templates: the WordPress page/post (or enabled custom-post) ID the template is for. Implies type page; one template per page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:829
msgid "Template technology. Sites normally have one: html."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:834
msgid "Whether the template is active. Disabled templates never render."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:838
msgid "Priority among templates whose rules match the same request; lower wins. Defaults to 10."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:843
msgid "Hook templates only: the WordPress hook name."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:848
msgid "Hook templates only: action or filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:852
msgid "Hook templates only: accepted args count. Defaults to 1."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:870
#: includes/features.php:918
msgid "Update template settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:871
msgid "Updates a Builderius template's registration-level settings through the builder's own updateTemplate mutation: title, slug, enabled state, type, sort order and apply rules (location + conditions). Only the fields passed change. This edits the same settings as the builder's template dialog — an open builder tab that later saves that dialog can overwrite these values, so prefer editing with the tab closed. Module content and CSS are separate (dbe/apply-subtree-html, dbe/patch-entity-css). Changes reach logged-out visitors immediately for apply rules and enabled state (they live on the post, not in a release)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:878
#: includes/abilities.php:917
msgid "Template post ID or slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:883
msgid "New slug."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:888
msgid "Template type: regular, page, doc or hook."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:909
msgid "Delete a template"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:910
msgid "Permanently deletes a Builderius template through the builder's own deleteTemplate mutation, including its branches and commit history. This cannot be undone — there is no trash for Builderius templates. Requires confirm: true; confirm with the user before calling. A published release that included the template keeps rendering its already-built output until the next dbe/publish."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:922
#: includes/abilities.php:1362
msgid "Must be true. Deletion is permanent; confirm with the user first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:945
msgid "Template (or component) post ID or slug for ENTITY-scoped variables. Omit to work on the GLOBAL settings set — data-variable-backed Collections usually bind global variables; literal JSON and URL sources do not need a data variable."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:951
#: includes/features.php:837
msgid "Get data variables"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:952
msgid "Reads Builderius dynamic-data variables from the saved state: the GLOBAL settings set by default (data-variable-backed Collections can bind these with data-b-context=\"[[name.path]]\" or data-b-context=\"[[[name.path]]]\"), or one template's entity-scoped variables when template is passed. Collections can also use literal JSON or URL sources when those resolve to arrays. Each entry has name, type (graphQLQuery, json, …) and value (the GraphQL query text or JSON). The `wp` entry is the system variable (flagged system: true) — the current post/user/menu context. Returns the branch and commit for the expected_commit save flow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:998
msgid "Create, update or delete a data variable"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:999
msgid "Creates, updates or deletes a Builderius dynamic-data variable in the saved state, committed through Builderius' own mutation. Works on the GLOBAL settings set by default (usual for data-variable-backed Collection loops) or one template when template is passed. Names are snake_case (the builder UI cannot edit camelCase names). graphQLQuery values are syntax-checked before saving; verify the query actually returns data on the rendered page afterwards (logged-in users see saved commits — no publish needed). Collections may also use literal JSON or URL sources when no data variable is needed. The system `wp` variable cannot be created, renamed or deleted; updating its query needs allow_system: true — that is the headless equivalent of the builder's dynamic-data helpers (e.g. adding nav_menu or metabox_value fields for settings pages). Read dbe/get-data-variables first for the current state and expected_commit. An open builder tab will not see the change until reloaded — and its own save can overwrite this; the dirty-tab preflight protects against that."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1010
msgid "The variable name. snake_case for create (e.g. team_data, never teamData)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1014
msgid "Update only: rename the variable (snake_case). Bindings using the old name are NOT rewritten."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1020
msgid "Create only: the variable type."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1024
msgid "The GraphQL query text (graphQLQuery) or JSON text (json). Required for create; optional on update (omit to keep the current value when only renaming)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1028
msgid "graphQLQuery only: GraphQL variables as a JSON object. Rarely needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1033
msgid "Required to update the system `wp` variable's query. Never allows renaming or deleting it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1041
msgid "Preview: validate and return the resulting variable without saving."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1056
msgid "The resulting variable (null after delete)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1071
msgid "Template (or component) post ID or slug for that entity's snippets — the right scope for page-specific behaviour. Omit for the GLOBAL settings set: site-wide snippets loaded on every Builderius page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1077
#: includes/features.php:842
msgid "Get JS snippets"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1078
msgid "Reads the Custom JS snippets from the saved state: the GLOBAL settings set by default (site-wide), or one template's snippets when template is passed. Each snippet has a label, generated id, code, and delivery options (external file vs inline, footer vs header, loading strategy, priority, enabled). Returns the branch and commit for the expected_commit save flow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1115
msgid "Create, update or delete a JS snippet"
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1116
msgid "Creates, updates or deletes a Custom JS snippet in the saved state, committed through Builderius' own mutation — the headless equivalent of the builder's JavaScript footer tool. Global scope by default (site-wide); pass template for page-specific snippets. Labels are snake_case (the builder UI cannot edit camelCase names). Defaults: served as a generated external file, in the footer, enabled. Write vanilla JS wrapped in DOMContentLoaded, use event delegation with data-* attribute hooks, and toggle CSS state classes rather than inline styles. Read dbe/get-js-snippets first for the current state and expected_commit. Saved snippets render for logged-in users immediately; logged-out visitors need dbe/publish."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1127
msgid "The snippet's label or id. For create, the new snippet's label (snake_case, e.g. faq_accordion)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1131
msgid "Update only: rename the snippet (snake_case). The generated id is stable across renames."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1135
msgid "The JavaScript source. Required for create."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1139
msgid "Insert in the footer (default true) or the header (false)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1143
msgid "Serve as a generated external .js file (default true) or as an inline script (false)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1148
msgid "Loading strategy for external snippets."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1153
msgid "Shown in the builder's snippet configure panel."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities.php:1157
